{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 90,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A prayer of Moses the man of God. LORD, thou hast been our dwelling-place in all generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou turnest man to destruction; and sayest, Return, ye children of men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a thousand years in thy sight ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as yesterday when it is past, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a watch in the night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a sleep; in the morning ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like grass ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " groweth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth; in the evening it is cut down, and withereth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we are consumed by thy anger, and by thy wrath are we troubled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast set our iniquities before thee, our secret ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "sins",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the light of thy countenance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For all our days are passed away in thy wrath: we spend our years, as a tale ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is told",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The days of our years ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seventy years; and if by reason of strength ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " eighty years, yet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their strength labor and sorrow; for it is soon cut off, and we fly away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who knoweth the power of thy anger? even according to thy fear, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So teach ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to number ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " days, that we may apply our hearts to wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Return, O LORD, how long? and repent thou concerning thy servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O satisfy us early with thy mercy; that we may rejoice and be glad all our days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make us glad according to the days ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast afflicted us, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the years ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " we have seen evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let thy work appear to thy servants, and thy glory to their children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.90.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yes, the work of our hands establish thou it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
